  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Vietnam - Strengthening Public Procurement Legislation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Development Objective is to strength the public procurement system through amending the existing legislation to remove the key shortcomings &amp; inconsistencies and to bring the legislation in line with international standards &amp; good practices; and building implementation capacity. A participatory approach will be used in development of the law and implementing decree based on the existing legislation.  The Government will use its own budget to finance related activities such as workshops, surveys, study tours, etc.  The IDF funds will be used to finance the following activities: 1. Consultant Services in Development of the Public Procurement Law and the Implementing Decree: To hire external consultants (international and national consultants) to help amend the existing laws and the related decrees &amp; regulations. 2. Training of Trainers: To provide training for trainers on the law and implementing decree. 3. Financial Audit of the IDF Grant: To hired qualified and independent auditors to conduct financial audit of the IDF grant with a view to ascertain that the grant funds have been used for the intended purpose and in line with the Grant Agreement.</narrative>
  </description>
